# LeakSanitizer Suppression File for jsec
#
# Policy: Keep zero broad library or prefix suppressions (such as leak:libssl,
# leak:libcrypto, leak:EVP_, leak:BIO_, leak:X509_, leak:CRYPTO_, or
# leak:janet_). LSan matches leak:<pattern> against any frame in the allocation
# call stack, so broad library or prefix rules mask jsec's own leaked OpenSSL
# objects and janet_malloc buffers.
#
# Only add narrow, exact function-symbol suppressions here if a specific
# third-party one-time initialization allocation is proven unavoidable on a
# target platform.